**File:** `components/screens-components/cart-items-section.tsx:31–39`

Every render creates **three new arrow functions per item**. If `CartItemCard` uses `React.memo`, the new references defeat memoization and every card re-renders on any quantity change anywhere in the cart.

```tsx
// PROBLEM — new function references every render
{items.map((item) => (
  <CartItemCard
    key={item.id}
    item={item}
    onIncrement={() => onIncrement(item.id)}   // new ref
    onDecrement={() => onDecrement(item.id)}   // new ref
    onRemove={() => onRemove(item.id)}         // new ref
  />
))}
```

**Fix:** Move the handlers into `CartItemCard` itself (it already receives `item.id`), or memoize the callbacks using a `useCallback` map keyed by id, or accept stable callbacks from the context directly.

```tsx
// Option: let CartItemCard close over its own id
<CartItemCard
  key={item.id}
  item={item}
  onIncrement={onIncrement}   // stable ref from useCallback in context
  onDecrement={onDecrement}
  onRemove={onRemove}
/>

// Inside CartItemCard:
const handleIncrement = useCallback(() => onIncrement(item.id), [onIncrement, item.id]);
```

