**File:** `components/screens/profile-screen.tsx:25–111`

`iconBox` is defined inside the component, so it's a new function every render. The `items` arrays passed to `ProfileSectionCard` are new object-literals every render. If `ProfileSectionCard` is or becomes memoized, this blocks it.

```tsx
// PROBLEM — new function, new arrays, new item objects every render
function iconBox(Icon: ...) {
  return <AppView>...</AppView>;  // new React element every call
}

items={[
  { key: 'orders', leading: iconBox(ClipboardList), onPress: () => router.push(...) },
  ...
]}
```

**Fix:** Move static item definitions outside the component. Use `useMemo` for items that depend on `tokens`, and `useCallback` for press handlers.

```tsx
// Outside component — no token dependency, icons are stable
const ACCOUNT_ITEMS_CONFIG = [
  { key: 'orders', title: 'Order History', Icon: ClipboardList, route: '/order-history' },
  ...
];

// Inside component — memoized
const accountItems = useMemo(() =>
  ACCOUNT_ITEMS_CONFIG.map(({ key, title, Icon, route }) => ({
    key,
    title,
    leading: <IconBox Icon={Icon} tokens={tokens} />,
    rightChevron: true,
    titleColorName: 'text' as const,
    onPress: () => router.push(route),
  })),
  [tokens]
);
```

